-- title:
--   Row form of Hecke compatibility for the supersingular residue pairing
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ with $5 \le p$ and an algebraically closed field $K$ of characteristic $p$, together with natural numbers $N \neq 0$ and a prime $\ell \neq 0$. The two function fields involved are $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldC K N`, the $K$-subfield of $K((q))$ generated by the $q$-expansions $j(q)$ and $j(q^N)$, and $F' =$ `charLDegeneracyRoof K N ℓ`, generated by $j(q)$, $j(q^N)$, $j(q^{\ell})$, $j(q^{N\ell})$; both are assumed to be curves over $K$ (principal divisors of degree zero, residue fields finite over $K$, $\Omega$ free of rank one) with canonical local residues, with $\Omega$ nontrivial, and with the differential $d(\pi_v)$ of a uniformiser spanning $\Omega$ at every place. Further hypotheses: $(N : K) \neq 0$, $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \neq p$, a unit $\zeta$ of $K$ that is a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity, an integer $m \ge 1$, integrality of the two degeneracy maps $\alpha =$ `heckeAlphaC` (the inclusion $F \hookrightarrow F'$) and $\beta =$ `heckeBetaC` (induced by $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$), a finset $SS$ of places of $F$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces p N K` (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in `ssJSet p K`), the hypothesis that for every place $w$ of $F'$ the restriction of $w$ along $\alpha$ lies in $SS$ if and only if its restriction along $\beta$ does, and a value vector $v$ on `SSIndex p N K hp5 (2m)`. The assertion is an equality of two $K$-valued functions on the subtype of those $\omega \in \Omega[F/K]$ satisfying $\mathrm{weightDivisor}_m(x) - 1 \le \mathrm{ord}_x(\omega)$ for every index $x$ of weight $2m$ and $\mathrm{weightDivisor}_m(x) \le \mathrm{ord}_x(\omega)$ for every $x \in SS$ whose width does not divide $m$, where $\mathrm{ord}_x(\omega)$ is the valuation of the coefficient of $\omega$ against $d(\pi_x)$. The first function sends $\omega$ to $\sum_{x \in SS}$ of the trace to $K$ of the local residue at $x$ of $g \cdot \partial_x\omega$, where $g$ is the chosen lift `liftFun` of the vector `ssHeckeFun p N K hp5 (2m) ℓ v` and the pairing uses the constant family $\mathrm{diagonalHom}(g)$; the second sends $\omega$ to the same residue sum over $SS$, taken against the lift `liftFun` of $v$ itself, of the differential $\mathrm{Tr}_{\beta}\bigl((\ell^{m-1} \cdot h^m) \cdot \alpha^{*}\omega\bigr)$, with $h =$ `heckeMultiplier N K ℓ` the element of $F'$ with $d(\beta(j)) = h \cdot \alpha^{*}(dj)$, $\alpha^{*}$ the Kähler pullback along $\alpha$ and $\mathrm{Tr}_{\beta}$ the differential trace along $\beta$.
--
--   This is the functional (row) form of the compatibility between the supersingular Hecke operator at $\ell$ in weight $2m$ and the residue pairing of bounded differentials against supersingular value vectors: the pairing of $T^{ss}_\ell v$ with $\omega$ equals the pairing of $v$ with the transposed correspondence $\mathrm{Tr}_{\beta}(\ell^{m-1}h^m \alpha^{*}\omega)$. It is used in the identification of the supersingular $\Theta$-map with the dual of that correspondence.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_ssResiduePairing_ssHeckeFun_eq_comp_traceAlong.lean

